🧠 Core idea (1 sentence)
Good code = less mental load, not just working output
🔑 The “secrets” simplified
1. Complexity = your real enemy
- Comes from:
  - too many dependencies
  - unclear logic (obscurity)
👉 Goal:
- reduce things you need to think about at once
2. Strategic vs Tactical coding
- Tactical = quick fix, hack, patch
- Strategic = design so problem doesn’t return
👉 Rule:
- short-term speed = long-term pain
3. “Deep” classes (very important)
- Bad:
  - small class, does little, exposes everything
- Good:
  - hides complexity inside
  - simple interface outside
👉 Think:
- small API, big power inside
4. Abstractions = layers
- Each layer should:
  - hide complexity below
  - expose clean logic above
👉 If layer adds confusion → it’s wrong
5. Comments = WHY, not WHAT
- Bad:
  - // increment i
- Good:
  - // retry to handle race condition from API delay
👉 Code shows what, comments explain why
6. “Define errors out of existence”
- Design system so errors can’t happen
Example:
- instead of checking null everywhere
- create type/system where null is impossible
👉 This is elite-level design thinking
7. Pull complexity downward
- High-level code:
  - should look simple
- Complexity:
  - hidden deep inside modules
👉 Top = clean
👉 Bottom = messy (but contained)
🧪 Meta insight (important)
- This is NOT a recipe system
- It’s:
  - spot bad patterns (red flags)
⚡ TL;DR (ultra short)
- reduce complexity
- design before coding
- hide complexity inside modules
- keep top-level code simple
- prevent problems instead of fixing them
